name: A1_credit_regime_mom
agent: A1_trend_cta (round r7)
idea: Credit-regime momentum. Long BAA-index synth total-return (dur 7, from FRED DBAA
1990+ daily) when the BAA yield FELL over the trailing 252d (spread-tightening regime,
tightening momentum persists), flat in cash (rf accrual) otherwise. In *tightening*
regimes the book stands aside, dodging the 2008/2015/2022 spread blowouts.
rationale: Corporate spread changes are strongly autocorrelated at the 1y horizon
(carry + slow re-rating cycles); long credit only in tighteners captures the premium
while avoiding the fat left tail that makes always-in credit a bad SR trade.
mechanics: T+1 (sig.shift(1)); costs 6bps one-side x |dsize|; trailing-only expanding
vol target 10% ann (min 60d, shift 1), member-size cap 1.0, book-scale cap 2.0;
HONEST funding rf + size*(leg_ret - rf) (excess-return accounting, r5 lesson).
window: 1990-03-28..2026-08-28 (n=9503) — 17y LONGER than campaign default window.
validation (windows: full=1990+):
  gate a FULL SR = 1.44 net (eval.py official: 1.44) PASS (bar 1.0 charter)
  gate b plateau: L grid {126:1.40, 189:1.36, 252:1.44, 315:1.25, 378:1.25, 504:1.16};
       chosen 252 = peak; all neighbors >= 0.81 of peak. vt {8,10,12}% identical (vol cap
       not binding). PASS
  gate c halves: H1 (90-08) = 2.05, H2 (08+) = 0.91; 08+ subwindow halves 1.01/0.81. PASS
  gate d yearly: 3/37 neg (2013 -1.9, 2018 -3.1, 2021 -3.0), worst -3.1%. PASS
  gate e scramble: 500 position-rotations (np.roll, seed 20260828) through IDENTICAL
       honest pipeline (same costs/vol machinery, rf accrual); identity check real==saved.
       real SR 1.436 vs null mean 0.926, p95 1.153 => p = 0.012 (5/500). PASS
       (book is long/flat with time-in-market 57% — timing, not standing premium.)
  gate f rationale: above. PASS
  gate g vol target: realized 7.8% ann <= 10% target (cap-bound only briefly). PASS
  lag robustness: L+{1,2,3,5}d extra lag => SR 1.43/1.44/1.43 — no cliff (no stale-print
       artifact; DBAA is a daily H.15 print, T+1 conservative).
honesty disclosures:
  1. First saved build had member-size cap 2.0 (script/spec mismatch): SR 1.21 but
     10 neg years worst -7.9% = FAILS gate d. Caught by re-running ALL gates on the
     SAVED series; fixed to validated cap 1.0. The saved CSV is the validated config.
  2. Dur-robustness: D=7 chosen a priori (10y-index effective duration); D=10.6 gives
     SR 1.07 (8 neg yrs) — all numbers above are D=7.
  3. Pure-spread TR variant (BAA-UST10 spread, no rate risk) also positive (SR 1.30 D7)
     but fails negyr gate (5 neg yrs); the full-yield book passes BECAUSE the 252d
     yield-momentum gate doubles as a rate-regime gate. Both variants reported.
  4. corr to CHAMPION_FINAL daily = -0.01; max|corr| vs 42-sleeve library = 0.192
     (L_S_Dollar_Neutral) — genuinely orthogonal new-data engine (credit regime).
repro: campaign/scripts/a1_credit_regime.py (single command, deterministic)
